From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 13:32:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04860/11362] [outer-loop] Policy: source-reading is a
 PUBLIC-games dev tool only, NEVER in the hidden live submission
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Operator directive 2026-06-29: "We only want to use the source-exposure probe for public games in our
conductor and outer loop, never for hidden games as part of our live agent submission." Encoded in the
ARC Live-Path Reachability Discipline (Self-solve provenance contract): reading game source / probing
source exposure / importlib-exec + set_level teleport + ground-truth win-flag is PERMITTED for the 25
public games in dev (conductor/outer-loop, offline_arcade, GameAdapters) but FORBIDDEN as any part of the
LIVE agent's hidden-game scored submission — the scored agent must self-discover hidden games from frames
+ exploration + induction. Removed the hidden-eval source-exposure probe kernel I had started building
(scripts/kaggle/source_exposure_probe_kernel) on this directive. Rationale: deliverable is live
self-discovery; source-reading on hidden games is the anti-pattern + metric-penalized (RHAE squares
efficiency) + DQ-risky; settled WITHOUT an empirical hidden-sandbox probe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
